                <pb facs="0537" n="509" xml:id="pg509"/>

                <head>232. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 3, President Eisenhower replied
                    to Prime Minister Kishi’s letter of
                    September 24 on the nuclear testing program. For texts of both letters, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 21, 1957,
                    pages 635 and 636, respectively. Documentation on the question of nuclear
                    testing appears in volume XIX. Additional documentation regarding Japan’s claims
                    for damages allegedly arising from the United States nuclear testing program is
                    in Department of State, Central Files 711.5611, 794.5, and 894.245.</p>
            </div>
